><country>JP</country><doc-number>10036865</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6158079-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6158079</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5366646-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5366646</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5560854-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5560854</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="WO-1994012594-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>WO</country><doc-number>1994012594</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1088883A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>JAPAN ENERGY CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAIMAI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN ENERGY CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAIMAI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAIMAI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAIMAI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A lubricant for compression refrigerating machines employing ammonia as a refrigerant, which contains a polyether compound and either an aromatic amine compound or a phenothiazine compound and preferably further contains an alcohol compound, such as a partially etherified polyhydric alcohol, and/or a benzotriazole compound.  Also provided are a hydraulic fluid composition comprising the lubricant and an ammonia refrigerant and a refrigerator filled with the hydraulic fluid composition. The lubricant not only has good compatibility with ammonia but is excellent in stability and lubricity. It is hence suitable for use in compression refrigerating machines employing an ammonia refrigerant, which has no fear of causing ozonosphere depletion or global warming.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un lubrifiant pour compresseurs frigorifiques utilisant l'ammoniac comme réfrigérant, renfermant un composé polyéther et soit un composé amine aromatique soit un composé phénothiazine, et renfermant également, de préférence, un composé alcool, et/ou un composé benzotriazole. L'invention concerne également une composition de fluide hydraulique contenant ledit lubrifiant et un réfrigérant à base d'ammoniac, ainsi qu'un réfrigérateur rempli de cette composition de fluide hydraulique. Le lubrifiant présente non seulement une bonne compatibilité avec l'ammoniac, mais également une excellente stabilité et un excellent pouvoir lubrifiant. Par conséquent, ledit lubrifiant peut être utilisé dans les compresseurs frigorifiques utilisant un réfrigérant à base d'ammoniac, qui ne risque pas de provoquer un appauvrissement de la couche d'ozone ou le réchauffement de la planète.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>